; the number of leaves in a tree equals the length of its flattened leaf list: count e = len(flatten e).
; count folds (+1 per leaf) over the Expr AST; flatten lists the leaves. By tree induction: Leaf -> 1 = len[v]; Node -> count l + count r = len(flatten l) + len(flatten r) [IHs] = len(flatten l ++ flatten r) [length homomorphism] = len(flatten(Node l r)). The SIZE bridge -- third of the flatten-homomorphism triad (eval<->sum value, mirror<->rev structure, count<->len size).
